{
  slug === 'open-source-self' && (
    <figure class="case-visual">
      <div class="visual-label">Archive architecture / one-way loop</div>
      <div class="visual-frame">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 800 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="self-title self-desc">
          <title id="self-title">Open-Source Self architecture</title>
          <desc id="self-desc">
            Raw conversations flow into a structured profile, then memory, then skills, then
            outputs. The first four layers stay private; only selected outputs are public.
          </desc>
          <g font-family="var(--mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--ink)">
            <rect x="24" y="26" width="172" height="42" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
            <text x="38" y="52">RAW ARCHIVE</text>
            <rect x="226" y="26" width="172" height="42" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
            <text x="240" y="52">PROFILE</text>
            <rect x="428" y="26" width="172" height="42" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
            <text x="442" y="52">MEMORY</text>
            <rect x="630" y="26" width="146" height="42" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
            <text x="644" y="52">SKILLS</text>
            <rect x="428" y="176" width="348" height="46" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" />
            <text x="442" y="204" fill="var(--accent-ink)">SELECTED OUTPUTS · PUBLIC</text>
          </g>
          <g fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.2">
            <path d="M196 47 H226" />
            <path d="M188 40 L196 47 L188 54" />
            <path d="M398 47 H428" />
            <path d="M390 40 L398 47 L390 54" />
            <path d="M600 47 H630" />
            <path d="M592 40 L600 47 L592 54" />
            <path d="M703 68 V176" />
            <path d="M696 168 L703 176 L710 168" />
            <path d="M96 68 V232 H428" stroke-dasharray="4 5" />
            <path d="M420 225 L428 232 L420 239" />
            <path d="M96 232 V252" />
          </g>
          <g font-family="var(--mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--muted)">
            <text x="24" y="92">63 SESSIONS · ~104 MB</text>
            <text x="226" y="92">2026-08-14</text>
            <text x="428" y="92">DURABLE RULES</text>
            <text x="630" y="92">39 FOLDERS</text>
            <text x="24" y="276">PRIVATE BY DEFAULT</text>
            <text x="428" y="248">METHOD + FINISHED WRITING</text>
          </g>
          <g stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="1" fill="none">
            <path d="M18 110 V244" stroke-dasharray="2 4" />
            <path d="M18 110 H26" />
            <path d="M18 244 H26" />
          </g>
          <g font-family="var(--mono)" font-size="9" fill="var(--muted)" transform="rotate(-90 10 177)">
            <text x="10" y="177">PRIVATE</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="visual-caption">
        The archive is a pipeline, not a portfolio. Each layer is dated, diffable, and readable by
        an assistant. Only the last box crosses the line.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

{
  slug === 'dobby' && (
    <figure class="case-visual">
      <div class="visual-label">Paragraph mode / inline gloss</div>
      <div class="mock-browser">
        <div class="mock-bar">
          <span></span><span></span><span></span>
          <div class="mock-url">reading.example/article</div>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-page">
          <p>
            The <ruby>experiment<rt>实验</rt></ruby> was designed to measure how quickly the
            system returned to <ruby>equilibrium<rt>平衡</rt></ruby> after the disturbance. The
            first run produced a <ruby>deviation<rt>偏差</rt></ruby> large enough to question the
            apparatus, not the theory.
          </p>
          <p class="mock-dim">
            The gloss sits above the word and leaves the English line intact. Nothing opens.
            Nothing replaces the page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="visual-caption">
        A reconstruction of the reading view. The Chinese is small and low-contrast on purpose;
        the English stays the object being read.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

{
  slug === 'learn-stuff' && (
    <figure class="case-visual">
      <div class="visual-label">Session transcript / entropy</div>
      <div class="mock-chat">
        <div class="mock-line mock-line--ai">
          <span class="mock-tag">TUTOR</span>
          <p>
            Imagine a sealed box split down the middle. Hot water on the left, ice on the right.
            Pull out the divider. What happens next?
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-line mock-line--you">
          <span class="mock-tag">LEARNER</span>
          <p>Heat moves from the hot side to the cold side until the whole box is the same temperature.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-line mock-line--ai">
          <span class="mock-tag">TUTOR</span>
          <p>Have you ever seen a lukewarm box split itself into a hot half and a cold half?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-line mock-line--you">
          <span class="mock-tag">LEARNER</span>
          <p>No. Energy conservation does not forbid it. It just never happens. Why?</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="visual-caption">
        The learner supplies the question that unlocks the concept. The tutor's job is to keep
        producing anchors, not answers.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

